#{[17592186069927 #edb/ref 1064 "To simplify a rational expression, we cancel out the largest common factor from the numerator and denominator. To do this, we sometimes need to factor the numerator and denominator before canceling.\n\nFor example, suppose that we wish to simplify $\\dfrac {4x - 12} {10x + 4}.$ To do this, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {4x - 12} {10x + 4}\n\t\t&=\\dfrac {4(x - 3)} {2(5x + 2)}\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot (x - 3)} {2(5x + 2)}\\[5pt]\t\t\n\t\t&=\\dfrac {\\cancel{2} \\cdot 2(x - 3)} {\\cancel{2}(5x + 2)}\\[5pt]\t\n\t\t&=\\dfrac {2(x - 3)} {5x + 2}\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069927 #edb/ref 1065 1370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069927 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "332f534f-811e-5c03-8393-560134dd4ea8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069927 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186073029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186073030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186073031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186073032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186073033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186073031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073028 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "723fead1-3866-508a-9080-2df0ed86113b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073029 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073029 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073029 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ff3933f1-5330-5a93-bd06-b1a968921e45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073030 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073030 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/r