17] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186074901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "71a6f31c-0bb8-5061-8779-9e3b7984d66e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074893 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074893 #edb/ref 1061 81656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074893 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ac8583b6-39eb-5a51-9b51-c3c4ebec13fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074893 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186075038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074894 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074894 #edb/ref 1061 81657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074894 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f054590d-449e-5753-b1fc-569c01699cad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074894 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074895 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074895 #edb/ref 1061 81660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074895 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aab5d8f4-9d49-5c7f-9619-01557ca3969b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074895 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074896 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074896 #edb/ref 1061 81663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074896 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bd74231b-139c-5091-8fd3-66103c7f1329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074896 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074897 #edb/ref 1061 81666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074897 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b13509a4-8a23-5240-a77b-f79cb3691c99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074897 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074898 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074898 #edb/ref 1061 8890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074898 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "123d2929-5563-5b7e-8588-e7734bb4eb42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074898 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074899 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074899 #edb/ref 1061 8891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074899 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f954535e-e2c6-5a01-85b8-f90fdccafc1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074899 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074900 #edb/ref 1061 8892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074900 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a335606-3bdb-5535-8956-9a3ababd7eb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074900 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074901 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074901 #edb/ref 1061 8895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074901 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1961bdcc-cea7-5d78-88c1-4f69e1dab833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074901 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074902 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074902 #edb/ref 1061 8947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074902 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d97c5e30-e125-5cba-9973-1e1898eca20e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074902 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074978 #edb/ref 1064 "The distance between two points in the coordinate plane is the number of units between them. Let's explore two methods for calculating the horizontal distance between two points with the points $(1,1)$ and $(5,1).$\n\n**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFirst, we plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/19/196c50295e8d8a95084c31226fb9319ede7b70603d894b6939e4615df583c29c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $4$ units, so the distance equals $4.$\n\n![](images/4b/4b531e29616f3e8d7ea0c65761e59cfea224b9c0e756c68b7647c7271dc09493.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/6d/6d5c6760e15098dc381e639cd806b6410f2fa6d9049d11d5467427635c9872b6.png)\n\nThe point $({\\color{blue}{1}},1)$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{1}$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $({\\color{red}{5}},1)$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{5}$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is ${\\color{red}{5}} - {\\color{blue}{1}} = 4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074978 #edb/ref 1065 2199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074978 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "aeee8d0d-20f6-5700-8c35-c66e0eef8daa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074978 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074979 #edb/ref 1064 "When we want to find the distance between two points in different quadrants, method 1 works exactly the same, but method 2 is slightly different.\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis for a horizontal distance, or $x$-axis for a vertical distance, and then *adding*. \n\nSo, what's the distance between $(-3,2)$ and $(1,2)?$\n\n**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/e0/e0fec8fca43b421b62efc3d6d892563c80beaab3c2816be47aa7563868555268.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $4$ units, so the distance equals $4.$\n\n![](images/dd/ddc1e6cec323fe245ff2a115a587e773d408dc0115ba5002c02ac1d238620c63.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/0b/0bbb91fc8c0e7ad577261dcdbc8e7aaa16a44e8be2e937e2d6870aae58af4ccf.png)\n\nThe point $({\\color{blue}{1}},2)$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{1}$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $({\\color{red}{-3}},2)$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{3}$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is ${\\color{red}{3}} + {\\color{blue}{1}} = 4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074979 #edb/ref 1065 2204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074979 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a1233efd-87e1-5707-9b70-24c24ed47418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074979 #edb/ref 1067 "The Distance Between Two Points in Different Quadrants" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075038 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's take a look at the following equivalent ratios:\n\n![](images/6c/6cda61e0fbd0d9695644a29f0c6fa3478eae84cf253623da7f4b544f35873472.svg)\n\nWe can place the equivalent ratios in a **ratio table**, such as the one below. In a ratio table, each row represents a ratio.\n\n| ${\\color{blue}5}$ | ${\\color{red}10}$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| ${\\color{blue}10}$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}\\textrm{?}}$ |\n| ${\\color{blue}20}$ | ${\\color{red}40}$ |\n\nOne number is missing. Let's figure out what it is.\n\nWe start with the ratio ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}10},$ which is the first ratio in the table. Writing this ratio as a fraction, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}}{{\\color{red}10}}.\n$$\n\nThe numerator represents the left-hand entry (${\\color{blue}5}$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry (${\\color{red}10}$).\n\nTo find the missing number, we need to make a numerator of ${\\color{blue}10}.$ We can do this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\times 2}{10\\times 2} & =\\frac{10}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now add this to our ratio table:\n\n| ${\\color{blue}5}$ | ${\\color{red}10}$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| ${\\color{blue}10}$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}20}$ |\n| ${\\color{blue}20}$ | ${\\color{red}40}$ |\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{red}20.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075038 #edb/ref 1065 8357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075038 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ca7b3d51-7281-5705-bed5-276f34939c25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075038 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095886 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "813aaeae-688c-5e88-936e-02dac71e1499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095916 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "03913dbe-158c-5e69-a492-f412ab726635" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095928 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/r